# Third-party content in this repository

Everything under `.claude/` is not one thing, and the difference matters when reading it.

## Written here

- `.claude/agents/ba.md`, `qa.md`, `ta.md`, `critic.md` — the agent chain this repository is
  about. Their design, their handoff contract and the artifacts they produce are the subject of
  `pipeline/` and of the README.

## Vendored, not ours

- `.claude/agents/playwright-test-planner.md`, `playwright-test-generator.md`,
  `playwright-test-healer.md`
- `.claude/skills/playwright-cli/`, `.claude/skills/playwright-component-testing/`,
  `.claude/skills/playwright-trace/`

These are Playwright tooling definitions shipped with Claude Code, vendored into the repository so
that a clone reproduces the same environment. They are included unmodified and are the property of
their respective authors. They are not part of what this repository claims as its own work, and
nothing in the MIT licence above is asserted over them.

📌 They are kept because reproducibility is the point: `CONVENTIONS.md` records that the CLI is the
first choice and MCP the fallback, and that decision is only checkable if the tooling it names is
present.
